# Engine patches are byte-exact artifacts (CRLF convention + deliberately CR-less
# lines before "\ No newline" markers -- THE PRE-MARKER CR RULE, 2026-07-21).
# autocrlf normalization would re-CRLF every line on checkout and break the
# forward --binary gate; store and check out their bytes verbatim.
memoria-patches/*.patch -text

# SFX sequence scripts + sfxmodel manifests are byte-exact deploy assets (sha256
# drift-guarded by the custom-summons study builds; the committed LF bytes are the
# live-deploy-proven ones). core.autocrlf smudged them to CRLF on checkout, which
# tripped every guard -- never line-end convert them (2026-07-22).
*.seq -text
*.sfxmodel -text

# Committed FBX (only minted-from-scratch exceptions escape the *.fbx ignore, e.g. NIMBRA's
# 6400.fbx): binary, byte-exact — never line-end convert.
*.fbx -text

# Rung 3's registered predictions are sha256-frozen (studies/story-trace/rung3_trace.py P-FROZEN): a session
# records the sha of the bytes it read, and the analysis refuses a file that no longer matches -- so a checkout
# that re-CRLFs one fails P-FROZEN with no content changed. The committed LF bytes are the recorded ones
# (v1: 220532a8); never line-end convert them.
studies/story-trace/rung3_predictions*.json -text
